<p>Reports an un-annotated parameter of a <code>@SpringBootTest</code> test-class constructor when the effective
<code>@TestConstructor</code> autowire mode is the default <code>ANNOTATED</code>.</p>

<p>In <code>ANNOTATED</code> mode Spring injects only constructor parameters annotated with <code>@Autowired</code>,
<code>@Qualifier</code> or <code>@Value</code>, so an un-annotated parameter is not resolved and the test fails at runtime.
Annotate the parameter with <code>@Autowired</code>, or opt the whole class into injection with
<code>@TestConstructor(autowireMode = TestConstructor.AutowireMode.ALL)</code>.</p>

<p><b>Example:</b></p>
<pre><code>
@SpringBootTest
class MyTest {
    // reports 'service': not autowired under the default ANNOTATED mode
    MyTest(MyService service) { }
}
</code></pre>
